    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But that's the thing... the \"resilience\" part feels like a fallacy. You say the universe doesn't work the way I expect, but the math actually says this is the natural state. Everything moves toward disorder. My life isn't a \"moment\" to be experienced, it's just a series of failures that's finally reaching its logical conclusion. It feels less like I'm struggling against chaos and more like I'm just part of the inevitable decay. Does it even make sense to keep fighting a mathematical certainty?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
